# 6. Data Preparation

Python was used to prepare the dataset before analysis.

The main data preparation steps included:

* Loading the dataset.
* Inspecting the dataset structure.
* Checking the variables and data types.
* Checking for missing values.
* Filtering the dataset to individuals aged **15–35**.
* Creating age groups for analysis.
* Examining employment-status categories.
* Checking education-level values.
* Handling missing education values where appropriate.
* Preparing the cleaned dataset for further analysis.

The age groups used in the project were:

| Age Range | Age Group     |
| --------- | ------------- |
| 15–19     | Adolescents   |
| 20–24     | Young Adults  |
| 25–29     | Early Workers |
| 30–35     | Prime Workers |

