# 17. Conclusion

This project analysed youth unemployment in Ghana by examining differences across gender, education, age, region, and urban-rural location.

Python was used for data preparation and exploratory analysis, while PostgreSQL was used to perform structured SQL analysis. A simple machine learning section was also included to demonstrate the application of machine learning to the unemployment dataset.

The project provided practical experience in data cleaning, exploratory data analysis, visualisation, SQL, database analysis, and introductory machine learning. It also helped demonstrate how data can be used to identify patterns in a real-world social and economic issue.

The findings and recommendations presented in this project are based on the available dataset and should therefore be interpreted within the limitations of the data.

